  definition used there: followed = Delta = ee_final/s >= 2; e_min = 2 s/G; Y if e_min <= e_need in all three settings.
  soundness: a signal-to-noise test of a bounded response (gain G = 2.4-115, racemic state stable) to a continuously supplied excess,
  against an e_need that comes from a bifurcation ramp (inherit.py). It says the readout tracks the feed excess above counting noise.
  It does not say the system selects one hand; the product excess stays below 1 for small seeds (see (c) ee-vs-yield).

